    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this was an upfront-quoted RYDE_XL fare, and the money turns on the ERP pass-through, not on the route. On the route, the trace measures 11.99 km against an optimal 12.2 km — an excess of -0.21 km, or -1.72% — so no deviation is established under POL-RD-01 and, this being an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip, POL-RD-11 closes the distance-and-time refund route in any event. The driver is right that the premise of a distance dispute fails, and the rider does not press for one. The driver's 'pooled itinerary' point also fails on the record: vehicle_type is RYDE_XL, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply. The fare ledger charged three ERP lines totalling SGD 14.00. Two of them were genuinely crossed — West link entry SGD 3.00 and Canal link exit SGD 3.00, each with a trace fix on the gantry coordinates at 0.0 m — and those SGD 6.00 are properly chargeable pass-throughs under POL-RD-09 and are not refunded. The third line, North service-loop ERP SGD 8.00, was charged as crossed but the trace's closest approach is 16,784.57 m, far outside the 250 m crossing radius; the driver never crossed it, so the line is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4) and is refunded in full. The refund is the POL-RD-11(a) figure, read off the fare ledger: charged_total 42.00 less quoted_fare 28.00 less properly chargeable pass-throughs 6.00 = SGD 8.00, which rounds up to SGD 8.00 unchanged and matches the ledger's own pol_rd_11_remedy. That is a single sum, not two: POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding the off-route pass-through correction on top of the POL-RD-11(a) figure, since the phantom line is already excluded from the properly chargeable total. The rider sought SGD 14.00; the evidence supports SGD 8.00, hence PARTIAL_REFUND. On the driver's chat reference to an 'air pollution fee sixty extra': no such line appears anywhere in the fare breakdown and nothing of the kind was billed, so it adds nothing to the chargeable total and the rider's point that no pollution fee was paid is correct. POL-RD-06 does not fire — deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed trips and there is no material deviation — so neither the POL-RD-06(b) uplift nor a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows; the driver's claim correctly confines itself to the two fields the clause names. No traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-00712-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0), and since the driver asserts no external traffic cause and cites no advisory, POL-RD-13 leaves POL-RD-03 unavailable without triggering escalation; no deviated or exculpatory limb turns on it here. Confidence is capped at 1.0, the minimum weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding facts (the fare ledger and the trace, each at 1.0); the missing advisory carries no fact and does not lower the cap. The referral below is a billing-integrity finding under POL-RD-09(4) and rides with the refund; it does not displace the money."
