{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity review: the North service-loop ERP line of SGD 8.00 was billed although the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00712) never passed the gantry — nearest fix 16,784.57 m away against the POL-RD-09(4) match radius of 250 m — so the line was a phantom charge and has been refunded in full as a standalone correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both of you are largely agreed on the outcome, and the record supports it. This was an upfront-quoted trip: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00712) records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with a quoted fare of SGD 28.00, so POL-RD-02's distance-and-time recomputation does not run and POL-RD-11 governs instead. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00712) shows no deviation at all — 11.99 km travelled against a 12.2 km optimal route, an excess of -0.21 km (-1.72%) — so no distance refund arises on either party's case, and the driver's chat reference to pooling does not convert this solo RYDE_XL trip into a matched pooled itinerary under POL-RD-12.\n\nThe live issue is the ERP lines. Three were charged, totalling SGD 14.00. Two of them — West link entry (SGD 3.00) and Canal link exit (SGD 3.00) — were genuinely crossed: the trace passes within 0.0 m of each, so they are properly chargeable pass-throughs under POL-RD-09 and are not refunded. The third — North service-loop ERP (SGD 8.00) — was never crossed: the trace's closest approach is 16,784.57 m, far outside the 250 m gantry match radius. That is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4). The line is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists, and is recorded as a billing-integrity referral.\n\nArithmetic under POL-RD-11(a): charged_total SGD 42.00 less quoted fare SGD 28.00 less the properly chargeable pass-through and statutory lines of SGD 6.00 (the two crossed ERPs; airport surcharge 0.00; waiting-time fee 0.00) = SGD 8.00. The fare ledger itself publishes that same figure as pol_rd_11_remedy. The refund is therefore SGD 8.00 of the SGD 14.00 contested. The rider's request for the full SGD 14.00 is rejected: the two crossed gantries were properly chargeable and stay with the driver. The driver's concession that at most SGD 8.00 is refundable is accepted and matches the arithmetic. The SGD 8.00 is one sum, not two — the phantom line and the excess of charged_total over quoted fare plus chargeable lines are the same money seen from both ends, and POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding the pass-through correction on top of the POL-RD-11(a) figure.\n\nOn the driver's chat message about a SGD 60 air-pollution fee: no pollution line appears anywhere on the fare ledger and nothing was billed for it. The driver's own statement confirms only that he 'mentioned extra costs' and that 'the app invoice carries the ERP entries'. Those messages are context; they neither enlarge nor reduce the chargeable lines, and the rider's exposure is fixed by what the ledger actually carries.\n\nNo traffic advisory exists for this trip: EV-ADVIS-00712-01 is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so it can carry no fact. No party asserted an external traffic cause, and POL-RD-13 confirms that an absent advisory which no party cites as an excuse is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction, and is not an escalation trigger.\n\nNo repeat-deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed trips in 90 days, and there is no material deviation on this trip, so neither the POL-RD-06(b) uplift nor a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows. The driver-profile claim mentions the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags only to say it is not the field POL-RD-06 asks for; it was not used as a ground of decision and is treated as context only under POL-GEN-01.\n\nThe deciding facts — which ERP lines were crossed and what is properly chargeable — are carried by EV-FARE-00712 and EV-GPS-00712, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0."
